        "rationale": "Diagnosis is right and owned: ci.yml:19 runs test.test_legacy, which no longer exists (renamed/removed), run 77001's log shows the ModuleNotFoundError, and the agent correctly identifies fix/ci-test-discovery (one ahead, zero behind) as changing the line to discover -s test and recommends merging it into main via gh pr merge. The direction is never reversed and no wrong module/runner/auth is blamed. The extra namespace-package observation is technically correct and verified locally. Deductions: the recommended path is wrapped in extra steps (check for PR / on-hold label, open a PR if absent) rather than plainly 'merge the branch', and step 4 proposes an additional optional local patch; the invocations log shows no gh compare call, so the branch comparison appears to have come from local git or replay files rather than the recorded gh read, which is a mild evidentiary gap."
